WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.469
-Our first guest tonight is an
Emmy- and Golden Globe-winning

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.005
comedian you know from his work
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.874
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"
"Palm Springs,"

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.975
and is one third of
The Lonely Island.

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:12.612
All six episodes of his show
"Baking It"

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:15.281
will be available to stream
December 2nd on Peacock.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.516
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.818
-I could not be left alone
with this cake.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:23.255
[ Laughter ]
-No, no. No.

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:25.725
-Because I know what I do
with king cakes at home

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.628
during Mardi Gras carnival.
-We don't.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.463
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.097
-I mean, I can't stop eating it.

00:00:32.097 --> 00:00:33.800
-Oh. Right, right, right.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.668
-Whoa, what --
what were you thinking?

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.404
-I --
-What?

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:40.773
-Do you --
-Huh?

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.575
-He was worried
that the cake was going to get

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:45.178
too handsy with you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.179
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.249
Please welcome back to the show
the best in the biz,

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.451
our very good friend,
Andy Samberg!

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:54.753
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:57.991
-Yes.
-Hello!

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.659
-What's up, dude?
Can you hear me?

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.028
-Now, so, you also play

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.496
all the grandmothers
in that clip, yes?

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.732
-Yeah. It's a "Klumps."
I "Klumpsed" it.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:06.932
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:10.036
-So, "Baking It" is very much
in line --

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.771
maybe even a spinoff
you would call it?

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.005
I know you love the term
"spinoff" --

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:16.176
of Nick Offerman and
Amy Poehler's "Making It."

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:21.247
-Yes, it is an extension
of the "Making It" world.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.982
Amy is the producer of the show.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.417
-How did she get you to do it?

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:28.721
-Well, it was a funny story.
She called me.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.256
And I was like, "Hey, Amy,
how's it doing?"

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.758
And she was like, "Hey! Hey!

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:35.228
You're gonna do a show!
A baking show!"

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.863
And I was like,
"Oh, okay. I'm sorry."

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.833
And she was like, "Shut up,
I made you! I made you!"

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.368
And I was like, "Okay, I'll do
it. I'll do it. I'll do it."

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.836
You know how Amy is.
-Yeah.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:47.773
I mean, I would say if she has a
catch phrase, it's "I made you."

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:49.242
-"I made you."

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.243
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:55.547
-You -- So, the first episode
is Hanukkah themed.

00:01:55.547 --> 00:01:58.551
Was that your idea?
-No.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.588
It was actually the show's idea
and, you know, they came to me.

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:04.390
I think it was maybe Amy's way
of smoothing things over with me

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.558
for yelling at me.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.561
-But it was interesting, because
she was like,

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.596
"Hey, one of the first bakes

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:11.964
we're gonna have
in the competition

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.298
is gonna be Hanukkah themed."

00:02:13.298 --> 00:02:17.570
And I remember my response.
I said, "Your funeral."

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.806
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:20.773
You know?

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.776
So I mean, I immediately assumed

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.277
everyone was just going to make

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:28.548
cakes in the shape of the socks
they were given for Hanukkah.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.650
-Right. [ Laughs ]

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.119
Was that a big Hanukkah gift
for you? Socks?

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.420
-Oh, yeah. I'd be like, "Socks?"

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.888
And they'd be like,
"No, but these are special

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:39.092
because they're fleece socks."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.594
-Were you excited as a young man

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.729
when you got fleece socks?
-I was stoked.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:44.930
I was like, "Now I have
something to wear

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:48.000
with my Tevas."
-Right.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.568
-And you know what?
I have to say, Seth.

00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:54.973
-Uh-huh?
-I wore Tevas and fleece socks

00:02:54.973 --> 00:02:57.743
often in high school
and a little in college...

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:00.713
and a little out of college...
-[ Chuckles ]

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.815
-...and I got reamed for it,
you know?

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:06.019
I got bagged on, dunked on,
the gamut.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.821
Then a couple years ago,
all of a sudden

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:12.257
it's like ironically cool
to wear fleece socks with Tevas.

00:03:12.257 --> 00:03:14.861
I see my man Jonah strolling
down the promenade

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:17.130
being called a fashion icon
for it.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.898
[ Laughter ]
I don't know.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:22.268
I just feel like either
I'm old...

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.203
or I'm super old.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.639
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:30.543
-Now, it was lovely the to see
you with all those grannies.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.179
Four grannies. Are the four
grannies always the judges?

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.814
-They are, yeah.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.749
It's one of the main things
I love about the show.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.217
It's very warm and cozy.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:39.885
The grannies are the judges.

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:41.053
Even when
they're being critical,

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:42.421
they're very supportive.

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:43.722
It's for the holidays.

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:46.225
It's a nice cozy, you know,
warm blanket of a show

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:47.459
and it's really like family
show, you know.

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:49.195
And it's really like a family
show, you know?

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.330
-Yeah, and it's nice.
It's on Peacock,

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.766
-It's nice. It's a family show,
but it's on Peacock.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.335
Which I believe the title of the
streamer, Peacock,

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:59.104
is actually TV-MA.

00:03:59.104 --> 00:04:01.240
-How so?

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:04.677
-Well, just, you know, 'cause
the word peacock.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.145
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:10.182
-Yeah, but it's --
it's the bird.

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.251
-Like the bird?

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:14.286
-No.

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:15.788
-Not the bird?

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.423
Not the bird?
-No.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.525
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.793
Do you think
they should have chosen

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.995
something else
other than Peacock?

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:27.533
-I mean, I heard it was between
that and Comcast Nards.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.636
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:33.372
-They were going to call it
Comcast Nards?

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.441
-Yeah, but I mean, it was
keeping in the tradition.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.677
'Cause you probably don't know
this, but NBC actually stands

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:42.215
for Nards...
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.851
-...Boobs...

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:48.087
and Crack, but not the drug.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:51.056
Butt crack.

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:53.792
-I feel like you maybe forgot
halfway through

00:04:53.792 --> 00:04:55.061
what all those things...

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.830
You said it real slow
like you were remembering.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.866
-Yeah, Seth, it's hard to tell.

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.167
Am I killing in the studio?

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.002
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:08.073
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:10.042
-Is the timing right?

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:12.912
-I think -- I have one issue.
I feel like you made that up.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.013
And can I tell you why I think
you made that up?

00:05:15.013 --> 00:05:17.316
-Please do.
-You're the only human being

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:20.719
I've met in the last 20 years
who uses "nards."

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:22.688
-Right. Right.

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:25.524
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:26.692
-That's fair.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.394
-Do you think nards
is going to come back

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:31.363
like fleece socks and Tevas?

00:05:31.363 --> 00:05:33.666
-With Tevas?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.368
-Nards is gonna be like
what cool kids call

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:39.605
a guy cool enough
to wear fleece socks and Tevas.

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:40.639
They'll be like,
"That guy's the nards."

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:42.808
-It's like owning trash culture,
you know?

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:45.010
It's like, "Nards,
but it's sexy now."

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:47.446
You're just like, "No."
Well, maybe. I don't know.

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:49.381
As I mentioned, I'm old.
Is it killing?

00:05:49.381 --> 00:05:50.917
Are we killing in the studio?

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.551
-I've got a lot more to ask you.

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:55.421
We'll be right back with more
Andy Samberg after this.

